    "purpose": "Reference values for measuring extraction quality (ANLS, CER, field-level P/R/F1, exact match).",
    "provenance": "Transcribed by reading each scan in samples/ directly. This is annotation, not an independent gold standard produced by a third party — it is stated plainly wherever the numbers are reported.",
    "scope": "Typed/printed acts only. Handwritten registers are a distinct, much harder recognition problem and are measured separately, never mixed into these figures.",
    "field_semantics": {
      "child.name / father.name / mother.name": "Given name(s) and family name in separate slots. Scored two ways: whether the right name was read at all (order-insensitive over the words), and whether each part landed in the correct slot. The act's word order (surname-first in Nigeria and Benin, given-first elsewhere) is a typographic convention and is not itself graded.",
      "child.dob": "ISO 8601. The act often writes the date in words; converting it is part of the task.",
      "child.gender": "OpenCRVS enum: male | female.",
      "birth_place": "Free-text place of birth exactly as the act words it."
    },
    "null_means": "Field genuinely absent from the document. Predicting a value for it counts as a hallucination."
  },
